Techniques Used for Better Results:

Chain Of Thought
- When to use: Complex classification, multi-step reasoning
- Improvements: How the agent reasoned in making decisions would show in the response
- Tips: Think about how you would make decisions or how you want the agent to make decisions

Few-shot
- When to use: You need consistent tone and response
- Improvements: Responses became more uniform and I was able to shape the responses and behaviors in ways I wanted
- Tips: If there are behaviors you especially don't like from your agent, you can shape them by giving them how to respond via few-shot examples
I was able to have the agent reference previous queries in newly created tickets using this ticket.

Structured Outputs
- When to use: Output needs to be easily parsable and uniform
- Improvements: I was able to create tickets using same formats everytime which would be easily parasable down stream 
- Tips: Creating classes for structure within class can be useful and allow even more uniformity and constraints

Tools:
- When to use: Agent needs data before answering, You need to extend what agent can/will do
- Improvements: I was able to get the agent to reference a database for more tailored responses
- Tips: Telling agent how to use the tool with descriptions can better shape the outcome